WEBVTT

00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:03.330
Possession?!

00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:09.780
Yes! A power granted us by Lord Amis!

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:16.570
To retain their wits 
even while possessed...

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:21.710
How are they not losing control?

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:31.800
We, the Sons of Destruction, use our
 heroes' powers flawlessly. Like tools.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:34.300
We're nothing like you!

00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:36.940
The Sons of Destruction?

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:41.250
Heroes aren't meant to be used like tools!

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:43.710
They fight alongside us on the battlefield!

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:46.190
What a stupid idea.

00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:49.540
Now, see if you can break through this one!

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:52.690
Dark Release!

00:00:55.750 --> 00:00:56.950
Shirley—

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:04.150
Witness my deathblow!

00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:08.750
You're weak! The Seven Knights are weak!

00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:10.460
Is this the best you can do?!

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:15.450
Really, this has become
 utterly one-sided...

00:01:15.930 --> 00:01:16.970
Boringly so.

00:02:50.710 --> 00:02:57.170
<b>Rivalry\h\h\h-Conflict-</b>

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:57.170
Monsters of destruction...

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:01.960
To think there was a Physis base 
 in the school as well...

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:06.080
And when Claire learned of it...

00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:11.070
Dark Ruler Chris!

00:03:11.650 --> 00:03:14.960
Manifest the true blade of 
vengeance here in my hand!

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:18.990
Come!

00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:20.790
This is for Claire.

00:03:21.490 --> 00:03:23.960
I'll destroy every last one of you!

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:32.290
They're suddenly stronger!

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:42.200
Is this because of the power
 Jive was talking about?

00:03:45.770 --> 00:03:46.700
Damn.

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:49.160
We can't let 'em hold us up here!

00:03:49.470 --> 00:03:53.420
They're going to keep destroying silver 
hourglasses if we don't stop them!

00:03:53.770 --> 00:03:55.670
They might be doing so as we speak.

00:03:56.180 --> 00:03:59.170
Then the guys in the volcano...

00:04:00.230 --> 00:04:02.330
Stay safe, everyone!

00:04:08.650 --> 00:04:10.840
Just as prophesied, indeed.

00:04:27.170 --> 00:04:30.490
Your arrival here...

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:35.020
will bring my plan to fruition.

00:04:38.410 --> 00:04:46.470
Now... reveal to me
 the true Son of Destruction.

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:52.040
Nemo!

00:04:52.630 --> 00:04:53.230
He's strong.

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:57.120
You're weak! Pitifully weak!

00:04:57.120 --> 00:04:59.230
Couldn't you make this 
a little more fun for us?

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:03.990
It's our first time fighting
while possessed, after all.

00:05:05.420 --> 00:05:07.740
Their power is too great for us to overcome.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:14.000
We, Lord Amis's chosen, are indeed superior!

00:05:15.740 --> 00:05:16.940
Reda.

00:05:16.940 --> 00:05:19.960
We haven't forgotten 
that pathetic display of yours.

00:05:20.810 --> 00:05:25.130
Just stand back there 
and watch us finish them.

00:05:25.580 --> 00:05:26.840
Do as you like.

00:05:27.370 --> 00:05:28.140
But...

00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:32.140
You shouldn't get distracted 
until you've won for sure.

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:35.630
Clever brat...

00:05:41.310 --> 00:05:42.320
Fool!

00:05:50.610 --> 00:05:52.170
Damn you!

00:05:58.330 --> 00:06:03.800
How dare you... treat me this way!

00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:07.790
All of you, begone!

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:11.930
Wait—

00:06:13.370 --> 00:06:16.680
Volux... You bastard!

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:18.940
I knew it.

00:06:18.940 --> 00:06:21.770
They're not working together at all.

00:06:21.770 --> 00:06:25.440
That means, regardless of how
 strong they are, this isn't hopeless.

00:06:31.790 --> 00:06:34.950
Listen up, guys! Remember 
that you're not fighting alone!

00:06:35.250 --> 00:06:37.900
We can all work together!

00:06:38.310 --> 00:06:40.460
Let someone else have your back!

00:06:40.890 --> 00:06:43.960
And I'll need your help too, Spike!

00:06:47.290 --> 00:06:48.970
Hang in there just a little longer...

00:06:51.060 --> 00:06:52.090
Jive!

00:06:56.150 --> 00:06:59.230
Reda! Do something already!

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:03.480
I thought you didn't need my help.

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:04.640
Shut up!

00:07:04.640 --> 00:07:06.570
You think now is the time for your—

00:07:10.230 --> 00:07:11.490
Wh-What is this?

00:07:13.170 --> 00:07:14.460
My possession...

00:07:15.470 --> 00:07:21.160
Why... can't I... control it anymore?!

00:07:23.340 --> 00:07:24.400
This is...

00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:28.180
They were likely keeping 
the possession in control

00:07:28.180 --> 00:07:30.380
via the total subjugation of their heroes.

00:07:30.600 --> 00:07:33.770
It wasn't something they 
could keep up forever.

00:07:34.510 --> 00:07:37.360
No! This isn't what he said!

00:07:37.780 --> 00:07:40.780
Why is this happening to us?!

00:07:41.430 --> 00:07:43.520
There's likely also more to it.

00:07:44.300 --> 00:07:47.150
The heroes were resisting them.

00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:50.060
They didn't want to be treated like tools.

00:07:50.060 --> 00:07:51.030
Right.

00:07:51.030 --> 00:07:52.560
Why?

00:07:52.560 --> 00:07:57.030
Heroes are meant to be used! 
How can they defy us?!

00:07:57.030 --> 00:07:59.170
This is nonsense!

00:07:59.170 --> 00:08:04.100
Heroes are just the remnants 
of old power clinging to this world!

00:08:04.100 --> 00:08:07.000
They're merely a power to be exploited...

00:08:07.710 --> 00:08:10.050
That's what Lord Amis taught us.

00:08:10.050 --> 00:08:12.730
You're wrong. That's not true.

00:08:13.140 --> 00:08:14.050
What do you mean?

00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:16.570
I didn't understand at first.

00:08:17.160 --> 00:08:21.060
But our heroes talk to us!

00:08:21.580 --> 00:08:24.100
We need to be willing to listen to them!

00:08:25.050 --> 00:08:27.060
Listen to them?

00:08:27.310 --> 00:08:30.160
Don't be afraid. Open your heart!

00:08:31.070 --> 00:08:33.200
Don't be fooled, Reda!

00:08:34.070 --> 00:08:36.610
Even after all this, 
you still want to test your luck?

00:08:36.610 --> 00:08:38.000
Don't be stupid!

00:08:38.470 --> 00:08:41.030
We were chosen by Lord Amis.

00:08:41.030 --> 00:08:43.830
Even if our bodies are brought low,

00:08:44.100 --> 00:08:47.330
we'll send you to the God of Destruction!

00:08:47.570 --> 00:08:49.280
Don't be absurd!

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:55.340
Show your loyalty to Lord Amis!

00:08:55.340 --> 00:08:56.840
I won't let you lay a finger on him!

00:09:00.910 --> 00:09:04.030
You... You're...

00:09:05.340 --> 00:09:06.580
Yes.

00:09:06.580 --> 00:09:09.260
And it's <i>because</i> I'm no normal human

00:09:10.110 --> 00:09:13.220
that I'll protect those who've accepted me!

00:09:13.220 --> 00:09:14.120
Nemo!

00:09:16.850 --> 00:09:19.320
Kaiser Phoenix!

00:09:23.490 --> 00:09:28.630
I beg your forgiveness, Lord Amis!

00:09:30.730 --> 00:09:33.500
Damn! This is insane!

00:09:33.500 --> 00:09:36.370
No... No, I don't want this!

00:09:39.060 --> 00:09:40.860
You're not human?

00:09:41.890 --> 00:09:43.880
I'll explain later.

00:09:44.450 --> 00:09:45.890
For now...

00:09:46.320 --> 00:09:47.930
We have one left to deal with.

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:51.490
You appear to have avoided a loss of control.

00:09:52.050 --> 00:09:53.400
But what do you plan to do now?

00:09:55.810 --> 00:09:57.140
Nemo, was it?

00:10:16.110 --> 00:10:17.580
This is unending!

00:10:17.580 --> 00:10:22.420
But to ensure Claire didn't die
 in vain, I must...

00:10:26.670 --> 00:10:27.890
Sophitia!

00:10:28.260 --> 00:10:29.430
What are you doing here?

00:10:29.430 --> 00:10:31.060
I'll explain later.

00:10:31.060 --> 00:10:33.110
For now, let's get you out of here!

00:10:33.450 --> 00:10:34.590
Understood!

00:10:35.520 --> 00:10:36.170
Nemo...

00:10:37.930 --> 00:10:40.850
Do you not realize the position you're in?

00:10:41.420 --> 00:10:43.650
Sorry, but with the three of us—

00:10:43.650 --> 00:10:44.310
Wait.

00:10:45.370 --> 00:10:48.760
Would the two of you head 
into the temple without me?

00:10:49.310 --> 00:10:51.420
Wait, are you serious?

00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:53.880
I'll be fine.

00:10:56.990 --> 00:11:00.180
Leave this to me.

00:11:02.110 --> 00:11:03.430
Very well.

00:11:03.430 --> 00:11:04.680
President!

00:11:05.080 --> 00:11:10.890
I'll grant that we must stop 
Physis's plan as soon as possible.

00:11:12.300 --> 00:11:15.820
But... I won't forgive you if you die.

00:11:17.130 --> 00:11:19.070
Yeah. Thanks.

00:11:20.860 --> 00:11:22.320
Very well.

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:25.800
You'd better catch up later, Nemo.

00:11:29.930 --> 00:11:31.080
You're sure about this?

00:11:32.140 --> 00:11:35.840
After all... you and I are like siblings.

00:11:38.380 --> 00:11:41.210
So you really are...

00:11:43.820 --> 00:11:45.430
Then tell me.

00:11:46.370 --> 00:11:48.470
Why did you betray us?

00:11:49.390 --> 00:11:51.200
You were a chosen one,

00:11:51.900 --> 00:11:54.480
just like us...

00:11:55.430 --> 00:11:56.980
Why did you cast that aside?!

00:11:59.190 --> 00:12:01.340
Because I made my own decision!

00:12:01.820 --> 00:12:03.200
I chose a new life!

00:12:04.730 --> 00:12:08.900
You really think we're allowed to do that?

00:12:10.060 --> 00:12:12.460
We were made to be this way!

00:12:12.910 --> 00:12:15.180
What do <i>you</i> think, Reda?

00:12:16.320 --> 00:12:17.670
I...

00:12:20.670 --> 00:12:23.180
I hope he'll be all right by himself.

00:12:23.680 --> 00:12:26.320
I'm sure he has a plan in mind.

00:12:26.750 --> 00:12:29.180
And we have bigger things to worry about.

00:12:30.210 --> 00:12:31.560
Amis Germain?

00:12:32.420 --> 00:12:33.090
Yes...

00:12:33.530 --> 00:12:37.690
And stopping his plan 
to destroy the silver hourglasses.

00:12:38.390 --> 00:12:42.690
It was their job to take 
the ritual site, correct?

00:12:43.130 --> 00:12:45.700
Jou and Gildan, yes.

00:12:45.930 --> 00:12:48.200
I'm worried about them, but...

00:12:48.510 --> 00:12:52.200
Let us trust in our fellow Seven Knights.

00:12:53.040 --> 00:12:56.000
<i>And in the key to our victory...</i>

00:12:56.770 --> 00:12:58.580
<i>I'm counting on you, Ellen.</i>

00:13:12.540 --> 00:13:13.810
You're not bad.

00:13:13.810 --> 00:13:16.310
If I've grown stronger,

00:13:16.310 --> 00:13:18.310
it's because of the others!

00:13:19.180 --> 00:13:21.400
That so-called team of yours?

00:13:22.520 --> 00:13:25.410
A concept foreign 
to artificial successors like us.

00:13:27.320 --> 00:13:32.330
"Think of your hero's power—and each other—
as nothing more than tools."

00:13:33.350 --> 00:13:35.510
That is what Lord Amis taught us.

00:13:37.090 --> 00:13:39.080
Do you still feel that way?

00:13:39.660 --> 00:13:40.780
I...

00:13:41.610 --> 00:13:43.740
I admit I've had my doubts.

00:13:44.650 --> 00:13:48.090
But if I give in to them...

00:13:48.300 --> 00:13:53.790
I'll be denying everything I am!
Everything I've ever been!

00:13:57.370 --> 00:13:58.520
It's too late!

00:14:01.130 --> 00:14:03.080
I can't call on my hero's power...

00:14:04.280 --> 00:14:07.080
It's true that you can't change the past.

00:14:07.080 --> 00:14:08.070
But...

00:14:08.070 --> 00:14:11.450
There's no reason you can't 
change how you live!

00:14:12.830 --> 00:14:14.200
Even for those of us...

00:14:15.850 --> 00:14:16.960
who aren't human?

00:14:16.960 --> 00:14:18.150
That's right!

00:14:26.370 --> 00:14:28.420
<i>I can't move.</i>

00:14:29.180 --> 00:14:31.430
<i>He's going to strike me... to kill me.</i>

00:14:32.090 --> 00:14:33.350
<i>Is this the end...</i>

00:14:34.080 --> 00:14:36.500
<i>to a life that was never real?</i>

00:14:37.330 --> 00:14:40.220
<i>No. You want to live.</i>

00:14:40.660 --> 00:14:41.700
<i>Am I wrong?</i>

00:14:42.530 --> 00:14:43.690
<i>This voice...</i>

00:14:44.510 --> 00:14:46.710
<i>If you wish to live, then fight!</i>

00:14:47.790 --> 00:14:50.530
<i>I acknowledge your will!</i>

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:54.760
<i>I, Immortal Empress Irene!</i>

00:15:01.840 --> 00:15:03.000
What is this?

00:15:04.760 --> 00:15:08.410
You heard the voice of your hero, didn't you?

00:15:10.010 --> 00:15:12.280
I didn't understand at first, either.

00:15:12.840 --> 00:15:18.940
But if you try to listen,
they'll respond to your will.

00:15:19.810 --> 00:15:23.090
I think that's why you didn't lose control.

00:15:26.820 --> 00:15:29.290
I must find out

00:15:30.750 --> 00:15:32.360
what Lord Amis truly wants.

00:15:34.070 --> 00:15:36.140
Why did he create us?

00:15:36.560 --> 00:15:38.620
Why is he making us fight?

00:15:40.620 --> 00:15:41.490
Very well.

00:15:46.250 --> 00:15:48.500
Let's go. Together.

00:15:51.110 --> 00:15:54.250
You're a kind person, aren't you?

00:15:54.250 --> 00:15:56.750
No, certainly not.

00:15:57.700 --> 00:15:59.100
I wonder about that.

00:16:02.590 --> 00:16:05.420
Because I'm not like you.

00:16:06.530 --> 00:16:08.650
I'm a terrible liar.

00:16:15.420 --> 00:16:18.370
Lord Amis! S-Save me!

00:16:19.180 --> 00:16:22.620
I thought we weren't 
supposed to lose control.

00:16:22.930 --> 00:16:26.780
I'm going to die like this, 
just like Castres!

00:16:27.360 --> 00:16:30.360
I don't want to! This isn't what I want!

00:16:32.190 --> 00:16:35.140
Then why <i>didn't</i> you die?

00:16:38.030 --> 00:16:39.310
What?

00:16:39.310 --> 00:16:43.140
You ordered us to fight!

00:16:43.540 --> 00:16:44.880
I did.

00:16:44.880 --> 00:16:49.140
And the survivor would be 
the true Son of Destruction.

00:16:50.010 --> 00:16:53.080
That is what was prophesied to me.

00:16:54.780 --> 00:17:00.370
But it appears that was none of you three.

00:17:00.370 --> 00:17:02.060
Wh-What do you...

00:17:03.800 --> 00:17:05.510
The chosen one,

00:17:06.080 --> 00:17:08.420
the true Son of Destruction...

00:17:08.420 --> 00:17:10.800
shall arrive here soon.

00:17:11.770 --> 00:17:14.170
What a truly auspicious occasion!

00:17:14.170 --> 00:17:15.510
Lord Amis...

00:17:16.390 --> 00:17:18.300
What are you saying?

00:17:18.690 --> 00:17:23.050
There are two things I never told you.

00:17:24.310 --> 00:17:28.090
The first is that you can only resist

00:17:28.090 --> 00:17:34.280
the loss of control in possession 
for a very short time.

00:17:36.460 --> 00:17:38.490
The second...

00:17:39.260 --> 00:17:44.450
is that I have nothing 
but contempt for you.

00:17:52.360 --> 00:17:54.520
Why...

00:17:56.790 --> 00:17:59.340
You are artificial creatures.

00:17:59.920 --> 00:18:03.130
Artificial heroes, worthy of scorn.

00:18:03.130 --> 00:18:05.640
Tools that are easily disposed of.

00:18:06.900 --> 00:18:10.810
There is only one true hero 
in the world right now.

00:18:11.540 --> 00:18:13.650
Me!

00:18:21.150 --> 00:18:23.260
Yes. Indeed.

00:18:24.870 --> 00:18:27.210
As you command.

00:18:33.780 --> 00:18:34.800
Is this the place?

00:18:41.370 --> 00:18:42.680
Amis Germain!

00:18:42.940 --> 00:18:45.680
We've come to put a stop to your plans!

00:18:47.770 --> 00:18:50.150
Rejoice!

00:18:50.150 --> 00:18:53.190
I've just received divine word!

00:18:53.830 --> 00:18:54.820
Divine word?

00:18:57.940 --> 00:18:58.840
Is that...

00:19:00.180 --> 00:19:02.320
You killed one of your own?

00:19:02.710 --> 00:19:07.750
You too shall be sacrifices...

00:19:08.250 --> 00:19:14.590
Sacrifices to bring the true 
Son of Destruction into this world.

00:19:21.930 --> 00:19:22.940
This can't be.

00:19:23.440 --> 00:19:26.620
And yet it is.

00:19:27.950 --> 00:19:32.970
We've been under a fatal misapprehension.

00:19:34.680 --> 00:19:36.890
Which means he's...

00:19:39.900 --> 00:19:40.900
Nemo is...

00:21:14.540 --> 00:21:15.990
Amis Germain.

00:21:15.990 --> 00:21:18.630
You used to be an important 
man in the empire.

00:21:18.630 --> 00:21:19.790
Why are you doing this?

00:21:19.790 --> 00:21:21.600
It was my lofty position

00:21:21.600 --> 00:21:25.090
that taught me the intolerable 
corruption of this world.

00:21:25.090 --> 00:21:28.160
We must dissolve the existing state

00:21:28.160 --> 00:21:31.610
and put a leader in place 
to build an ideal society...

00:21:32.080 --> 00:21:34.930
A new hero!

00:21:35.450 --> 00:21:38.020
What a terribly simplistic idea.

00:21:38.020 --> 00:21:40.060
I take it you would be that leader, then?

00:21:40.060 --> 00:21:41.750
The Seven Knights...

00:21:41.750 --> 00:21:44.070
Running dogs of a bygone era.

00:21:44.070 --> 00:21:47.130
I shall now deliver your divine punishment

00:21:47.130 --> 00:21:51.330
in the name of the great Nestra!

00:21:51.330 --> 00:21:52.080
Incoming!

00:21:53.330 --> 00:21:55.910
Hunt them down, Blades of Destruction!

00:22:01.880 --> 00:22:02.710
Lightning!

00:22:07.970 --> 00:22:09.010
Did we do it?

00:22:09.010 --> 00:22:12.390
No, the leader of Physis 
wouldn't be undone so easily!

00:22:16.390 --> 00:22:17.600
He's unharmed?

00:22:17.600 --> 00:22:18.760
This is terrible!

00:22:18.760 --> 00:22:22.650
He's not even possessed like 
those three from before...

00:22:22.650 --> 00:22:25.770
My body is eternal and invincible.

00:22:25.770 --> 00:22:29.250
Your powers, borrowed from others, 
are like the toys of children!

00:22:30.030 --> 00:22:31.080
You're bluffing.

00:22:31.080 --> 00:22:33.410
No one is eternal!

00:22:48.340 --> 00:22:49.130
Got you!

00:22:50.350 --> 00:22:53.810
As I told you, I'm invincible.

00:23:01.170 --> 00:23:02.190
Is that...

00:23:09.480 --> 00:23:10.380
Shirley!

00:23:10.990 --> 00:23:14.120
Was that... time manipulation?

00:23:14.330 --> 00:23:15.990
Indeed it was.

00:23:15.990 --> 00:23:18.440
The power of the silver hourglasses...

00:23:18.440 --> 00:23:21.000
The power to control time!

00:23:25.640 --> 00:23:27.650
Goodness! Would this be 
the final confrontation?

00:23:27.650 --> 00:23:30.940
If we strike down Physis's leader,
 the battle will be over.

00:23:30.940 --> 00:23:34.800
We cannot allow another tragedy.

00:23:34.800 --> 00:23:36.680
Next time: "End Times."

00:23:35.490 --> 00:23:40.250
<b>Conclusion -End Times-</b>

00:23:36.680 --> 00:23:39.430
Every action has a consequence.
